🚀 What is GitOps in Kubernetes?

GitOps is a way of managing your Kubernetes cluster using Git as the single source of truth.

👉 Instead of manually running kubectl apply, you:

1)Store all your Kubernetes YAML files in Git
2)Use a tool that automatically syncs Git → Kubernetes cluster

Code change → Git push → Tool detects → Auto deploy → Cluster updated → Continuous sync


🎯 Key Point

👉 Everything is automatic after Git push
👉 No need for manual deployment
👉 Cluster is always controlled by Git

        👨‍💻 Developer
              │
              │  (1) Update YAML (deployment.yaml)
              ▼
        📂 Git Repository (GitHub)
        (Desired State Stored)
              │
              │  (2) Git Push
              ▼
   🔄 GitOps Tool (Argo CD / Flux)
   - Watches Git continuously
   - Detects changes
   - Compares states
              │
              │  (3) Auto Sync
              ▼
     ☸️ Kubernetes Cluster
     (Actual State Updated)
              │
              │  (4) Running Pods/Services
              ▼
        📦 Application Running

---------------------------------------------------

🔁 Continuous Loop (Self-Healing):

Kubernetes Cluster (changed manually ❌)
              │
              ▼
GitOps Tool detects drift
              │
              ▼
Re-sync from Git ✅
              │
              ▼
Cluster restored to correct state

