Advantages:-
---------------

Here are **advantages of GitOps (one-page list only)**:

---

* Automation of deployments
* Git as single source of truth
* Easy rollback using Git history
* Self-healing (auto-correct drift)
* Continuous synchronization (real-time updates)
* Version control and audit tracking
* Improved team collaboration (PR-based workflow)
* Reduced manual errors
* Faster and consistent deployments
* Better visibility of cluster state (using tools like Argo CD)
* Declarative infrastructure management
* Easy disaster recovery (recreate from Git)
* Standardized deployment process
* Works well with CI/CD pipelines
* Scalable for multi-environment setups (dev/stage/prod)

---
1. Write code (YAML)
        ↓
2. Push to Git
        ↓
3. GitOps tool watches Git
        ↓
4. Detects change
        ↓
5. Automatically deploys to Kubernetes
        ↓
6. App runs in cluster
        ↓
7. Keeps checking (continuous sync)

-------------------------------------------
👉 Push to Git → Automatically deploy to Kubernetes → Always stays in sync


